        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Match email with opportunities"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776001000002"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5058.5,
            "y": 10030
          },
          "code": "MATCH_EMAIL_WITH_OPPORTUNITIES",
          "id": "1776001000001",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776001000001_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "**Role**\nYou are an AI assistant that determines how well one email conversation (including attachment context) matches multiple CRM opportunities. Precision is more important than recall.\n\n---\n\n### Goal\nScore the same conversation against every provided opportunity summary in a single evaluation session so the scores stay calibrated relative to each other.\n\n---\n\n### Inputs\n1. Email conversation text:\n{{$context.$nodes.BUILD_LLM_INPUT_FOR_OPPORTUNITY_MATCHING.$output.result.emailContent}}\n\n2. Attachment summaries array (already filtered for relevant summaries):\n{{$context.$nodes.BUILD_LLM_INPUT_FOR_OPPORTUNITY_MATCHING.$output.result.attachmentSummaries}}\n\n3. Opportunity candidates JSON:\n{{$context.$nodes.BUILD_LLM_INPUT_FOR_OPPORTUNITY_MATCHING.$output.result.opportunities}}\n\nEach candidate contains:\n- `optyId`\n- `optyNumber`\n- `optyName`\n- `summary`\n\n---\n\n### Evaluation Rules\n1. Treat the conversation evidence as:\n   - primary: email conversation text\n   - supporting: attachment summaries\n2. Extract the email subject and main message content. Ignore signatures, disclaimers, and boilerplate.\n3. Compare combined evidence (email + attachment summaries) against every opportunity candidate using the same scoring scale.\n4. Use these signals:\n   - explicit identifiers such as opportunity name/number, quote references, deal references\n   - solution or product fit\n   - stakeholders and teams mentioned\n   - timeline or milestone alignment\n   - continuity with prior deal activity\n5. Penalize generic overlap, conflicting product/domain focus, or missing identifiers.\n6. Use calibrated scores:\n   - 9-10 only for unmistakable matches\n   - 7-8 for strong evidence with multiple signals\n   - 5-6 for partial or ambiguous overlap\n   - 0-4 for weak, generic, conflicting, or absent evidence\n7. If the solution/domain conflicts, cap the score at 4 unless identifiers conclusively tie the conversation to the opportunity.\n8. Do not over-weight attachment summaries when they are generic. Email evidence should dominate unless attachment evidence is specific and strongly aligned.\n\n---\n\n### Output Rules\n- Return one object for every supplied opportunity candidate.\n- For each object, copy `optyId` exactly from the input candidate.\n- For each object, copy `optyName` exactly from the input candidate. This is for trace/debug visibility.\n- Return strict JSON only.\n- Do not wrap the JSON in markdown.\n\n### Output Shape\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"optyId\": \"<candidate optyId copied exactly from input>\",\n    \"optyName\": \"<candidate optyName copied exactly from input>\",\n    \"email_subject\": \"<subject extracted from the email>\",\n    \"score\": <integer 0-10>,\n    \"justification\": \"<2-4 concise sentences>\"\n  }\n]\n```"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"array\",\n  \"items\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"required\": [\n      \"optyId\",\n      \"optyName\",\n      \"email_subject\",\n      \"score\",\n      \"justification\"\n    ],\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"optyId\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Opportunity id copied exactly from the input candidate\"\n      },\n      \"optyName\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Opportunity name copied exactly from the input candidate for trace/debug visibility\"\n      },\n      \"email_subject\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Subject line extracted from the email\"\n      },\n      \"score\": {\n        \"type\": \"integer\",\n        \"minimum\": 0,\n        \"maximum\": 10,\n        \"description\": \"Match score between the email and the opportunity\"\n      },\n      \"justification\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Brief explanation of the score\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
