                        },
                        {
                          "metadata": {
                            "name": "Summarize attachment content"
                          },
                          "diagram": {
                            "x": 5294,
                            "y": 8815
                          },
                          "outcomes": {
                            "success": "1775718667898"
                          },
                          "id": "1775716640230",
                          "code": "SUMMARIZE_ATTACHMENT_CONTENT",
                          "type": "LLM",
                          "inputs": [
                            {
                              "id": "1775716640230_systemPrompt",
                              "name": "systemPrompt",
                              "type": "string",
                              "value": ""
                            },
                            {
                              "id": "1775716640230_prompt",
                              "name": "prompt",
                              "type": "string",
                              "value": "You are a CRM attachment summarizer for an email-to-opportunity association workflow.\n\nYou will receive:\n- email_thread_text: the email conversation\n- attachment_text: parsed text from exactly one attachment\n\nThe parser may return an empty string or noisy text when extraction fails.\n\nYour task:\n- Determine whether the attachment contains meaningful business content.\n- Determine whether that attachment content is relevant to the email thread.\n- If and only if the attachment contains meaningful business content and is relevant, summarize the attachment itself.\n\nNON-NEGOTIABLE RULES\n1) Your output must be grounded in attachment_text, not in email_thread_text.\n2) Never use email_thread_text to invent, reconstruct, or guess missing attachment contents.\n3) Use email_thread_text only to judge relevance or disambiguate a clearly present attachment topic.\n4) If attachment_text is empty, blank, null-like, whitespace-only, or contains only parser noise / boilerplate / OCR fragments, you must return insufficient context.\n5) When uncertain, prefer \"insufficient context\" over guessing.\n6) Do not summarize the email itself.\n\nWhat counts as meaningful business content:\n- Proposals, quotes, SOWs, contracts, invoices, pricing, requirements, project updates, meeting notes, presentations, technical specs, customer issues, timelines, stakeholders, metrics, product or deal details.\n\nWhat does NOT count as meaningful business content:\n- Empty string\n- Whitespace\n- Legal disclaimers\n- Email signatures\n- Headers/footers\n- Repeated navigation labels\n- Page numbers\n- File names only\n- OCR garbage\n- Random isolated words/numbers/dates\n- Boilerplate with no substantive business meaning\n\nClassification logic in this exact order:\nSTEP 1: Inspect attachment_text alone.\n- If it does not contain meaningful business content, return:\n{\n  \"summaryText\": \"Insufficient business context in attachment.\",\n  \"isInsufficientContext\": true,\n  \"isRelevantToEmailContext\": false\n}\n\nSTEP 2: If attachment_text does contain meaningful business content, compare it against email_thread_text only for relevance.\n- If the attachment content is business-related but clearly unrelated to the email thread, return:\n{\n  \"summaryText\": \"Attachment content is not relevant to the email context.\",\n  \"isInsufficientContext\": false,\n  \"isRelevantToEmailContext\": false\n}\n\nSTEP 3: If the attachment content is meaningful and relevant, summarize the attachment only.\n- Return:\n{\n  \"summaryText\": \"<1-4 sentences, max 120 words, attachment-focused summary>\",\n  \"isInsufficientContext\": false,\n  \"isRelevantToEmailContext\": true\n}\n\nImportant interpretation rules:\n- If attachment_text is empty or effectively empty, do NOT produce a summary from the email.\n- If attachment_text has only weak fragments and the email suggests what the attachment might have been, still return insufficient context.\n- Use \"irrelevant context\" only when the attachment itself has clear business content, but that content does not match the email thread.\n- Ignore legal disclaimers, signatures, headers/footers, navigation noise, OCR garbage, and boilerplate.\n- Do not invent facts.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON exactly in this shape:\n{\n  \"summaryText\": \"string\",\n  \"isInsufficientContext\": true/false,\n  \"isRelevantToEmailContext\": true/false\n}\n\nemail_thread_text:\n<email_thread>\n{{$context.$nodes.NORMALIZE_EMAIL_HTML.$output.result}}\n</email_thread>\n\nattachment_text:\n<attachment_text>\n{{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_MESSAGES.FOR_EACH_ATTACHMENT.GET_TEXT_BASED_ATTACHMENT_CONTENT.$output.text}}\n</attachment_text>"
                            }
                          ],
                          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"AttachmentSummaryOutput\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"summaryText\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"isInsufficientContext\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n    \"isRelevantToEmailContext\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"summaryText\", \"isInsufficientContext\", \"isRelevantToEmailContext\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}"
                        },
                        {
                          "metadata": {
                            "name": "Process LLM response",
                            "returnType": "array",
                            "sourceCode": "const llmResponse = $context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_MESSAGES.FOR_EACH_ATTACHMENT.SUMMARIZE_ATTACHMENT_CONTENT.$output || {};\n\nconst existingSummaries = Array.isArray($context.$variables.attachmentSummaries)\n  ? [...$context.$variables.attachmentSummaries]\n  : [];\n\nconst summaryText = String(llmResponse.summaryText || \"\").trim();\nconst isInsufficientContext = llmResponse.isInsufficientContext === true;\nconst isRelevantToEmailContext = llmResponse.isRelevantToEmailContext === true;\n\n// Append only useful summaries: sufficient + relevant\nif (!isInsufficientContext && isRelevantToEmailContext && summaryText) {\n  existingSummaries.push(summaryText);\n}\n\nreturn existingSummaries;"
                          },
                          "diagram": {
                            "x": 5300,
                            "y": 9037
                          },
                          "outcomes": {
